This fixture fabricates HttpdConn / HttpdHeader graphs directly in inline-C
(there is no server, so no worker to reclaim them) to exercise the accessors
without spinning up sockets. Those fake conns -- and the small owned Strings
some(...) holds -- are never released, so LeakSanitizer reports them. They are
an intentional, bounded, process-lifetime leak in the TEST HARNESS, not in the
httpd-req-*-opt accessors themselves. The compiler/codegen path (emit-c /
build) is still leak-checked; only the spawned program opts out.
